1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. c4 {Kaufman's Variation,
honoured with a bare mention in M.C.O.} Be7 6. d4 O-O 7. Bd3 d5 8. O-O Nc6 9.
cxd5 Qxd5 10. Re1 Ng5 $2 ({Of course} 10... Nf6 {is correct.}) 11. Nxg5 ({
I consider} 11. Bxg5 Bxg5 12. Nc3 (12. Be4 Qd8 13. d5 $16 {Stockfish 15}) 12...
Qd8 13. d5 {is even stronger.}) 11... Bxg5 12. Nc3 Qd8 13. d5 Bxc1 14. Rxc1 Ne7
15. Qh5 {White had a marked pull. Black's defences held, however, and a drawn
ending was eventually reached. 32 moves. Source: BCM, July 1950, p216} 1/2-1/2

